%--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
% readme_Lorenz_System_escape_Lc.txt
%--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Here we compute the statistics of escape time (from
% chaotic attractor) for NGRC DDE system learned from the Lorenz system;
% We compute these statistics for various values of imposed CLE (Lc); the
% case without imposing CLE is also included;
%--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Lorenz_scan_esc_Lc_aut_v2t.m -> In this file we first learn the NGRC DDE system
% from the Lorenz system, and then we integrate the closed NGRC system for various 
% initial cond-ns; the CLE (Lc) is scanned, and we thus get the dependence of statistics
% of escape time (from chaotic attractor) for various Lc values;
%--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The used par-ters (for NGRC DDE):
% h=0.01; tau=0.15; bet=1e-7; degree=7; Ndel=5;
% NTpr=1000; (number of num-cal exp-nts for each Lc value);
%--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Lorenz_signal.m -> this function computes the time series x(t) for the
% exact Lorenz system; this function is used in the file 
% [Lorenz_scan_esc_Lc_aut_v2t.m];
%--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
% These files are auxiliary functions for the NGRC DDE system:
%----------------------------------------------------------------------------
% generate_all_exp_matreces.m
% generateCheb_feat_vect.m
% generateChebyshevs.m
% generateChebyshevsDiffLyap.m
% genExponents.m
%----------------------------------------------------------------------------
% matr.mat -> contains power matrices necessary for composing Tschebyshev
% polynomials;
